# Frontend & CSS Standards - Unblock

## 🎯 REGLA DE ORO: DaisyUI Semantic Colors ALWAYS

**NEVER use hardcoded colors in HTML/Blade templates (except emails).**

### ❌ WRONG (hardcoded colors):
```html
<!-- BAD: Hardcoded hex colors -->
<div style="background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.95); border-color: #d1d5db;">
<svg style="color: #ca8a04;">
<button class="bg-blue-500 text-white">
```

### ✅ CORRECT (DaisyUI semantic colors):
```html
<!-- GOOD: Semantic classes -->
<div class="bg-base-100 border-base-300">
<svg class="text-warning">
<button class="btn btn-primary">
```

---

## 📋 DaisyUI Semantic Color Classes

Always use these semantic classes that adapt to theme automatically:

### Background Colors
- `bg-base-100` → Main background
- `bg-base-200` → Slightly darker background
- `bg-base-300` → Even darker background
- `bg-primary` → Primary brand color
- `bg-secondary` → Secondary color
- `bg-accent` → Accent color
- `bg-neutral` → Neutral color
- `bg-info` → Info color
- `bg-success` → Success color
- `bg-warning` → Warning color
- `bg-error` → Error color

### Text Colors
- `text-base-content` → Main text color (adapts to theme)
- `text-base-content/70` → 70% opacity text
- `text-primary` → Primary brand text
- `text-secondary` → Secondary text
- `text-accent` → Accent text
- `text-info` → Info text
- `text-success` → Success text
- `text-warning` → Warning text
- `text-error` → Error text

### Border Colors
- `border-base-300` → Border color
- `border-primary` → Primary border
- `border-error` → Error border

### Component Classes
- `btn btn-primary` → Primary button
- `btn btn-ghost` → Ghost button
- `input input-bordered` → Input field
- `card bg-base-100` → Card component

