## 📧 Email Templates - Special Case

**EXCEPTION**: Email HTML templates CANNOT use DaisyUI (email clients don't support modern CSS).

### Rules for Email Templates:

1. **Use INLINE STYLES only** (not `<style>` tag classes)
   - Email clients override `<style>` tag rules
   - Inline styles have maximum specificity

2. **Use neutral, professional colors**
   - Blue palette: `#3b82f6`, `#2563eb`, `#1e40af` (professional, universal)
   - Grey palette: `#f8fafc`, `#e2e8f0`, `#64748b` (neutral backgrounds)
   - Avoid brand-specific colors that may change

3. **Test in Mailpit IMMEDIATELY**
   - Don't assume CSS works in emails
   - Use Playwright Browser MCP to view: `http://0.0.0.0:8025`

4. **Use Tailwind Semantic Font Sizes** (even in inline styles)
   - NEVER use arbitrary font sizes like `13px`, `11px`, `42px`
   - ALWAYS use Tailwind's semantic scale values

### Tailwind Font Size Scale (for Email Inline Styles):

| Semantic Class | Pixel Value | Usage in Emails |
|---------------|-------------|-----------------|
| `text-xs` | `12px` | Footer text, copyright, fine print |
| `text-sm` | `14px` | Small text, labels, secondary content |
| `text-base` | `16px` | **Default body text** (most readable) |
| `text-lg` | `18px` | Emphasized body text |
| `text-xl` | `20px` | Small headings |
| `text-2xl` | `24px` | Section headings |
| `text-3xl` | `30px` | Large headings |
| `text-4xl` | `36px` | **OTP codes, important numbers** |
| `text-5xl` | `48px` | Hero text (rarely in emails) |

### ❌ WRONG (arbitrary sizes):
```html
<p style="font-size: 13px;">Company Name</p>  <!-- NOT IN SCALE -->
<div style="font-size: 42px;">123456</div>     <!-- NOT IN SCALE -->
<span style="font-size: 11px;">© 2025</span>   <!-- NOT IN SCALE -->
```

### ✅ CORRECT (Tailwind semantic sizes):
```html
<!-- text-xs (12px) for company name -->
<p style="font-size: 12px;">Company Name</p>

<!-- text-4xl (36px) for OTP code -->
<div style="font-size: 36px;">123456</div>

<!-- text-xs (12px) for copyright -->
<span style="font-size: 12px;">© 2025</span>
```

### Why This Matters:
1. **Visual consistency** between web UI and emails
2. **Predictable hierarchy** - everyone knows `text-sm` is smaller than `text-base`
3. **Easier maintenance** - changing from `text-sm` to `text-base` is semantic, not arbitrary
4. **Better accessibility** - Tailwind sizes are optimized for readability

### Email Template Pattern:

```html
<!-- CORRECT: All styles inline -->
<div style="background: linear-gradient(135deg, #3b82f6, #2563eb); padding: 40px 30px 30px 30px;">
    <h1 style="color: #ffffff; margin: 0; font-size: 24px;">Title</h1>
</div>

<div style="padding: 30px;">
    <p style="font-size: 16px; color: #555555; margin: 0 0 20px 0;">Text</p>
</div>
```

