## 🛠️ Email Template Overrides

When you publish vendor views (like `one-time-passwords`):

```bash
php artisan vendor:publish --tag=one-time-passwords-views
```

The template goes to:
```
resources/views/vendor/one-time-passwords/mail.blade.php
```

**CRITICAL**: Laravel Mail adds inline styles automatically via markdown/mail components. To prevent overrides:

1. **Use inline styles** in your Blade template
2. **Don't rely on CSS classes** defined in `<style>` tag
3. **Test in Mailpit** after every change

